                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e90b866e-3a48-3d3e-88b6-d5351e672e72",
                        "entry_id": "ce1cf8de-2554-3e26-822b-347dcff7580c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Matière animale sécrétée par les glandes placées sous la peau de l’abdomen du castor, femelle ou mâle, entre l’origine de la queue et la partie postérieure des cuisses, et qui est employée en médecine comme antispasmodique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b5812a-be63-4e69-a8c0-95d550f62928",
                                "sense_id": "e90b866e-3a48-3d3e-88b6-d5351e672e72",
                                "text": "Pour les uns, « ça sent le bitume ». Une autre voit ressurgir l’odeur « des gros feutres » utilisés sur les tableaux blancs. Tour à tour, la vingtaine de personnes installées dans la salle des fêtes de Velles (Indre) tendent leur nez au-dessus d’un flacon : à l’intérieur, du castoréum, une substance secrétée par le plus gros rongeur d’Europe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32cdd10b-0fbe-4b46-b3fd-4b554d683f9c",
                                "sense_id": "e90b866e-3a48-3d3e-88b6-d5351e672e72",
                                "text": "La seule observation que je ferai sur ces analyses , c’est que Brandes a pu se tromper sur la nature des castoréums qui en font le sujet, et que celui qu’il nomme castoréum de Russie pouvait être du castoréum du Canada, et réciproquement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "392c99c5-f3d9-4947-85b3-c5a44d8e2c12",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce1cf8de-2554-3e26-822b-347dcff7580c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e90b866e-3a48-3d3e-88b6-d5351e672e72",
                        "target_lang_word": "castoreum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "castoreum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3143df6-3a8b-32a1-acb4-0ae37e5fde98",
                                        "entry_id": "27b6d40a-6250-3fc5-8d0b-4ab7c42cf933",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The bitter exudate of the castor sacs of mature beavers, used as a scent mark, and as a tincture in some perfumes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3bf6135-918c-4e2b-95ea-304c72754664",
                                                "sense_id": "f3143df6-3a8b-32a1-acb4-0ae37e5fde98",
                                                "text": "One of the substances tried was castoreum.[…]If I were to judge from my own experience, I would say castoreum has very little therapeutic power, for I have not seen much benefit from its employment in those cases to which this remedy is said to be adapted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e28f3db-5827-47d9-b157-2afcb8f2ad2b",
                                                "sense_id": "f3143df6-3a8b-32a1-acb4-0ae37e5fde98",
                                                "text": "While the role of castoreum as a means of territorial advertisement has been extensively investigated and supported, the possibility of coding for sex information has not yet been excluded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a33a42f9-497e-4b1d-a473-780e1f853b28",
                                                "sense_id": "f3143df6-3a8b-32a1-acb4-0ae37e5fde98",
                                                "text": "Synthetic castoreums are now available, and can be as good as the natural fragrant^([sic])."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94217e52-2f13-45cd-9704-0773ef6ba6f8",
                                                "sense_id": "f3143df6-3a8b-32a1-acb4-0ae37e5fde98",
                                                "text": "Real oud is complex material, with honey, tobacco, leaf, minty-fresh and castoreum animalic notes all mixed together."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "081ab9bb-393a-3718-8be3-1e52d1be71ab",
                                        "entry_id": "27b6d40a-6250-3fc5-8d0b-4ab7c42cf933",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hat made from beaver fur."
                                        ],
